    },
    "displayName": "[A][M] Momentary Fortress",
    "version": 2,
    "subtype": "sage",
    "details": [
      {
        "type": "image",
        "value": {
          "image": {
            "url": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/rpg-pbp.appspot.com/o/games%2F1WLk8WgaysyvKtNs5P0a%2Fimages%2FXXQh3ed90t3lzn025wCz.png?alt=media&token=aa168f21-60b4-4b62-98d9-68d7d172e508",
            "tokenCrop": {
              "aspect": 1,
              "width": 100,
              "x": 0,
              "unit": "%",
              "y": 0,
              "height": 100
            }
          }
        },
        "visibility": "full"
      },
      {
        "type": "description",
        "value": {
          "description": "*You can create a protective pyramid, sphere, or cube of light around you that is able to repel physical and magical attacks.*\n\nDuring a Fight, you can use the Fortress to attempt to block one inbound physical or magical Attack against you each Turn.\n- If the Attack targets a Battlefield Area (like a magic blast) then everyone in the same Area as you benefits from the Fortress… including foes!\n\nIf cast outside of combat, the Fortress can be used to block harmful environmental effects. For example, Impact Damage from falling rocks or Burn Damage from caustic gas.\n\nThe Fortress is only visible when struck or resisting a harmful effect. The Fortress can be erected during your enemy’s Turn, but this means you cannot take an Action on your next Turn.\n\n**Requires a Contest**\nYour Insight vs. the Aptitude related to the type of Attack (see below).\n- **Magic Attacks:** The opposing Aptitude used should be the one required to cast the offensive spell.\n - If none is specified, use the caster’s Grit for directed attacks or Aura for harmful radiating attacks (or anything else!).\n- **Strength Attacks:** The opposing Aptitude for Melee Weapons, and other brute force attacks, should be the Attacker’s Might.\n- **Skill Attacks:** The opposing Aptitude for Missile Weapons, and other attacks that utilise finesse, should be the Attacker’s Deftness.\n- **Success:** The Attack is blocked, or dissipated, by a wall of impenetrable light. If successful, the Fortress remains intact and you benefit from its protection in the next Turn.\n- **Failure: **The panel of light shatters like glass, and the Fortress cannot be used again for 24 hours."
        },
        "visibility": "full"
      },
      {
        "value": {
          "range": "Gain 1 Bright Allegiance Point."
        },
        "visibility": "full",
        "type": "range"
      }
    ],
    "type": "abilities",
    "effects": [],
    "id": "f8KLPzlq0tu0pcA5mcjn"
  },
  {
    "privacy": {
      "users": [],
      "level": "private"
    },
    "details": [
      {
        "visibility": "full",
        "value": {
          "image": {
            "url": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/rpg-pbp.appspot.com/o/games%2F1WLk8WgaysyvKtNs5P0a%2Fimages%2FdJwCtjP4Bb4a3f2suTeg.png?alt=media&token=dba082a5-e19f-476c-98b2-c06c0e19baff",
            "tokenCrop": {
              "aspect": 1,
              "x": 0,
              "width": 100,
              "y": 0,
              "unit": "%",
              "height": 100
            }
          }
        },
        "type": "image"
      },
      {
        "type": "description",
        "visibility": "full",
        "value": {
          "description": "*You’re a true hunter, able to find a path through any built-up defense.*\n\nYou can attempt to find a weak spot on an opponent that is the target of your Hunter’s Focus.\n\n**Requires an Insight Check**\n**Success**: You can ignore any Defense Bonus the Target has from Armor and Speed Rating."
        }
      }
    ],
    "subtype": "raider",
    "displayName": "[A] Wind Wears Away Stone",
    "version": 2,
    "type": "abilities",
    "effects": [],
    "id": "fkRfxGfRWGZ0DG1q4x3q"
  },
  {
    "privacy": {
      "users": [],
      "level": "private"
    },
    "effects": [],
    "type": "abilities",
    "details": [
      {
        "value": {
          "image": {
            "url": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/rpg-pbp.appspot.com/o/games%2F1WLk8WgaysyvKtNs5P0a%2Fimages%2FU5vD1BJuto1FFJpws6wQ.png?alt=media&token=36a9ca31-c50a-4234-8b2a-5046d44229bc",
            "tokenCrop": {
              "aspect": 1,
              "x": 0,
              "width": 100,
              "y": 0,
              "unit": "%",
              "height": 100
            }
          }
        },
        "visibility": "full",
        "type": "image"
      },
      {
        "type": "description",
        "visibility": "full",
        "value": {
          "description": "*When the heat of the battle is upon you, the red mist descends and your rage takes control. This is very bad news for your foes... but your allies should be careful too.*\n\nYou can enter Berserk Mode while fighting or participating in a Check or Contest that calls for brute force.\n\nWhile Berserk, the following applies:\n- +2 on Attack rolls.\n- -1 to Defense Rating.\n- +2 Might and Grit.\n- You are unable to communicate or participate in any coordinated actions or team efforts. \n\nAfter you’ve dispatched a foe, or completed the objective of your Check or Contest you will:\n- Attack the closest individual in the same Battlefield Area as you, whether it’s friend or foe. \n- Continue to find and Attack targets until none are left.\nYou can attempt to exit Berserk Mode at the end of your Turn.\n\n**Ending Berserk Mode requires an Aura Check**\n- **Success**: You regain control.\n- **Failure**: You must wait until the end of the next Round before you can make another attempt to exit Berserk Mode."
        }
      }
    ],
    "displayName": "[A] Berserker",
    "version": 2,
    "subtype": "champion",
    "id": "h6kKR8KeG7jwWy1bOXSl"
  },
  {
    "privacy": {
      "users": [],
      "level": "private"
    },
    "effects": [],
    "type": "abilities",
    "details": [
      {
        "visibility": "full",
        "value": {
          "image": {
            "url": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/rpg-pbp.appspot.com/o/games%2F1WLk8WgaysyvKtNs5P0a%2Fimages%2F2TmcUnDWj1QjKNrHMm85.png?alt=media&token=55af5c92-e577-40db-87ee-f9dd8a900a34",
            "tokenCrop": {
              "height": 100,
              "unit": "%",
              "y": 0,
              "width": 100,
              "x": 0,
              "aspect": 1
            }
          }
        },
        "type": "image"
      },
      {
        "value": {
          "description": "*When physical force fails, you resort to psychological assault. By ridiculing your opponent’s deeply held beliefs, or competence, you can send your foe into an unbalancing rage.*\n\nOnce per Fight, you can attempt to enrage your opponent with a disparaging or spiteful truth. Targets for this Ability must:\n- Be engaged in a Fight with you for a Turn or more.\n- Be able to understand you.\n- Be capable of feeling emotions.\n\n**Requires a Contest**\nYour Grit vs. your opponent’s Aura.\n**Success**: Your comment unsettles your opponent: \n- Their rage now provides them with an Edge on all Attack rolls and Abilities aimed at you, but… \n- This leaves them open to attack. All Attack rolls made against the enraged foe benefit from an Edge. \n- Their rage ends if you die, are no longer visible, or when the current Fight ends.\n\nThis Ability may only be used on one opponent per Fight, whether it is successful or not."
        },
        "visibility": "full",
        "type": "description"
      },
      {
        "value": {
          "range": "Gain 1 Dark Allegiance Point."
        },
        "visibility": "full",
        "type": "range"
      }
    ],
    "displayName": "[S][M] Caustic Truth",
    "version": 2,
    "subtype": "murder princess",
    "id": "iGh5HnIVgUAX86wyHrVC"
  },
  {
    "type": "abilities",
    "effects": [],
    "details": [
      {
        "value": {
          "image": {
            "tokenCrop": {
              "aspect": 1,
              "x": 0,
              "width": 100,
              "y": 0,
              "unit": "%",
              "height": 100
            },
            "url": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/rpg-pbp.appspot.com/o/games%2F1WLk8WgaysyvKtNs5P0a%2Fimages%2FwX87fAYjqIHi8IRvr2Nx.png?alt=media&token=22b1044e-888f-4725-b0a1-04512dcc9473"
          }
        },
        "visibility": "full",
        "type": "image"
      },
      {
        "value": {
          "description": "*Your compassion can manifest itself as a protective force for your allies. This might take the form of an iridescent aura or a heart-shaped crystal shield.*\n\nOnce per Fight you can bestow an ally within your sight a force field that can absorb 1 Heart of Damage, after which it disappears. You can perform this Ability in addition to any other Actions permitted on your Turn.\n- **Rank 1**: You can Shield 1 person.\n- **Rank 4**: You can Shield 2 people.\n- **Rank 8**: You can Shield 3 people.\n\nIf you can protect more than one person, you can allocate your Shields in one go, or as required."
        },
        "visibility": "full",
        "type": "description"
      }
    ],
    "displayName": "[S][M] Shield of Love",
    "version": 2,
    "subtype": "battle princess",
    "privacy": {
      "level": "private",
      "users": []
    },
    "id": "iqSwLs327a5eGhYdCvnc"
  },
  {
    "effects": [],
    "type": "abilities",
    "displayName": "[S][M] The Widow Prisma",
    "subtype": "heretic",
    "version": 2,
    "details": [
      {
        "value": {
          "image": {
            "tokenCrop": {
              "height": 100,
              "unit": "%",
              "y": 0,
              "width": 100,
              "x": 0,
              "aspect": 1
            },
            "url": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/rpg-pbp.appspot.com/o/games%2F1WLk8WgaysyvKtNs5P0a%2Fimages%2FnnQmtyusTbZHfvbCzAt2.png?alt=media&token=97807d51-a4d8-4c1a-8941-3e87513336ce"
          }
        },
        "visibility": "full",
        "type": "image"
      },
      {
        "type": "description",
        "visibility": "full",
        "value": {
          "description": "*Prisma, The Crystal Martyr suffers for the chosen, although her curious moans while doing so suggest she receives some strange pleasure from her sacrifice.*\n\nUpon a cry for help, The Widow Prisma will immediately crystalize in front of you and absorb any inbound Attack.\n- Summoning is instantaneous.\n- Prisma suffers any Damage, Ailment, or detrimental effect directed at you… then dies.\n- Her dramatic death throes last a Turn, until she shatters into fragments and disappears.\n\nPrisma can only be summoned once every 24 hours."
        }
      },
      {
        "value": {
          "range": "Gain 1 Dark Allegiance Point."
        },
        "visibility": "full",
        "type": "range"
      }
    ],
    "privacy": {
      "level": "private",
      "users": []
    },
    "id": "jpxVnQw7O4ojTCwqrCmd"
  },
  {
    "privacy": {
      "level": "private",
      "users": []
    },
    "type": "abilities",
    "effects": [],
    "version": 2,
    "subtype": "raider",
    "displayName": "[S] Hunter's Focus",
    "details": [
      {
        "visibility": "full",
        "value": {
          "image": {
            "tokenCrop": {
              "unit": "%",
              "y": 0,
              "height": 100,
              "aspect": 1,
              "width": 100,
              "x": 0
            },
            "url": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/rpg-pbp.appspot.com/o/games%2F1WLk8WgaysyvKtNs5P0a%2Fimages%2FAxWu1TnZS0a3KMzGzWhv.png?alt=media&token=d1b94ead-63d8-4257-a9ae-c701676f8b3e"
          }
        },
        "type": "image"
      },
      {
        "visibility": "full",
        "value": {
          "description": "*The chaos and clamor of battle do not muddy your predatory instinct. Once your gaze has singled out a target, all distraction melts away and only your prey remains.*\n\nOnce per Fight you can choose a target for your Hunter’s Focus. You can do this at any time during the Fight.\n- Your Focus can be an opponent, but could also be an object you wish to destroy.\n- You cannot switch your Focus, even after your original target has been defeated or pacified.\n- You gain an Edge on all Attack rolls made against your Focus.\n\nYour GM can grant you an Edge on Checks and Contests that get you closer to dispatching your Focus.\n- For example, leaping over a chasm to get within striking distance."
        },
        "type": "description"
      }
    ],
    "id": "kRAGxPxR3qbkIHUz602c"
  },
  {
    "privacy": {
      "level": "private",
      "users": []
    },
    "version": 2,
    "displayName": "[S] Compassion Cure",
    "subtype": "battle princess",
    "details": [
      {
        "type": "image",
        "value": {
          "image": {
            "url": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/rpg-pbp.appspot.com/o/games%2F1WLk8WgaysyvKtNs5P0a%2Fimages%2FwX87fAYjqIHi8IRvr2Nx.png?alt=media&token=22b1044e-888f-4725-b0a1-04512dcc9473",
            "tokenCrop": {
              "y": 0,
              "unit": "%",
              "height": 100,
              "aspect": 1,
              "x": 0,
              "width": 100
            }
          }
        },
        "visibility": "full"
      },
      {
        "type": "description",
        "value": {
          "description": "*Your kind attention is so sincere that it can dispel ill effects. Your hug can lift a dispirited companion, your tears can thaw a petrified ally.*\n\nWith a touch, you can attempt to remove a psychological, physical, or magical Ailment from someone you care about.\n- Attempting this Ability during a Fight requires you to spend your Action.\n- This Ability cannot be used for situational Ailments: Toppled, Restrained, and Overburdened.\n\n**Requires an Aura Check**\n**Success**: The Ailment is removed.\n**Failure**: The Ailment remains, you cannot make any further attempts to cure it."
        },
        "visibility": "full"
      }
    ],
    "effects": [],
    "type": "abilities",
    "id": "md0Yz9eJfOrbkKbBVWHQ"
  },
  {
    "effects": [],
    "type": "abilities",
    "details": [
      {
        "visibility": "full",
        "value": {
          "image": {
            "tokenCrop": {
              "height": 100,
              "y": 0,
              "unit": "%",
              "x": 0,
              "width": 100,
              "aspect": 1
            },
            "url": "https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/rpg-pbp.appspot.com/o/games%2F1WLk8WgaysyvKtNs5P0a%2Fimages%2FOugkCJGuUh33HfAWIh9N.png?alt=media&token=64780a26-dc17-4ad3-b44b-b63a659e340f"
          }
        },
        "type": "image"
      },
      {
        "value": {
          "description": "*You can seize another’s shadow and, by proxy, their physical agency. While you make menacing gestures, resembling those of a puppeteer, your victim dances to your desire.*\n\nYou can use this Ability on any creature that casts a shadow and is roughly 10 feet, or 1 Battlefield Area, away.\n\n**Requires a Contest**\nYour Insight vs. your target’s Aura.\n- **Success:** You can control your target for the next 10 seconds, or their Turn during a Fight. For example, you can make them speak, shout, or even attack themselves (which still requires an Attack roll!).\n - You must repeat, and win, the Contest each Turn to retain control of your target.\n - You can only control one Puppet at a time.\n- **Failure:** The target breaks free of your mana strings and you cannot target them with this Ability again for 24 hours."
        },
        "visibility": "full",
        "type": "description"
      },
      {
        "visibility": "full",
        "value": {
          "range": "Gain 1 Dark Allegiance Point."
        },
        "type": "range"
      }
    ],
    "subtype": "sage",
